    assistant: "Ang **endangered species** ay mga hayop at halaman na nasa panganib ng extinction (pagkawala sa mundo). Ang Pilipinas ay isa sa mga biodiversity hotspots sa mundo, pero marami sa ating native species ay nanganganib na!\\n\\n**Bakit Maraming Endangered Species sa Pilipinas?**\\n\\n**1. High Biodiversity:**\\n- **7,641 islands** = isolated ecosystems = unique species\\n- **52,177 described species** (half endemic - wala sa ibang bansa!)\\n- **15th sa 17 megadiverse countries** sa mundo\\n- Pero high biodiversity + high threats = high extinction risk\\n\\n**2. Habitat Loss:**\\n- **Deforestation**: Forest cover bumaba mula 70% (1900) hanggang 24% (2024)\\n- **Urbanization**: Land conversion para sa settlements, industries\\n- **Agriculture**: Clearing ng forests para sa farming\\n- **Mining**: Destruction ng habitats\\n\\n**3. Hunting at Poaching:**\\n- Illegal wildlife trade\\n- Bushmeat hunting\\n- Collection para sa pet trade\\n- Traditional medicine\\n\\n**4. Pollution:**\\n- Pesticides nakakalason sa wildlife\\n- Plastic pollution sa marine species\\n- Water pollution sa freshwater species\\n\\n**5. Climate Change:**\\n- Changing habitats\\n- Coral bleaching\\n- Extreme weather events\\n\\n**Mga Endangered Species sa Pilipinas:**\\n\\n**Mammals (Mamalya):**\\n\\n**1. Philippine Eagle (Pithecophaga jefferyi):**\\n- **Status**: Critically Endangered (IUCN Red List)\\n- **Population**: 400 pairs na lang sa wild\\n- **Threats**: Deforestation, hunting, electrocution\\n- **Habitat**: Old-growth forests sa Sierra Madre, Mindanao\\n- **Conservation**: Philippine Eagle Foundation, breeding program, protected areas\\n- **Fun fact**: Pambansang ibon ng Pilipinas, isa sa pinakamalaking eagles sa mundo!\\n\\n**2. Tamaraw (Bubalus mindorensis):**\\n- **Status**: Critically Endangered\\n- **Population**: Less than 600 individuals\\n- **Location**: Mindoro lang (endemic)\\n- **Threats**: Hunting, habitat loss, diseases mula sa livestock\\n- **Conservation**: Mounts Iglit-Baco Natural Park, anti-poaching patrols\\n- **Fun fact**: Dwarf buffalo, mas maliit kaysa carabao!\\n\\n**3. Philippine Tarsier (Carlito syrichta):**\\n- **Status**: Near Threatened\\n- **Location**: Bohol, Samar, Leyte, Mindanao\\n- **Threats**: Habitat loss, pet trade, tourism disturbance\\n- **Conservation**: Philippine Tarsier Foundation, ecotourism\\n- **Fun fact**: Isa sa pinakamaliit na primates sa mundo, may eyes na mas malaki kaysa sa brain!\\n\\n**4. Philippine Mouse-Deer (Pilandok) (Tragulus nigricans):**\\n- **Status**: Endangered\\n- **Location**: Balabac Islands, Palawan lang\\n- **Population**: Unknown, declining\\n- **Threats**: Hunting, habitat loss\\n- **Fun fact**: Pinakamaliit na hoofed mammal sa mundo!\\n\\n**5. Dugong (Dugong dugon):**\\n- **Status**: Vulnerable\\n- **Location**: Coastal waters, especially Palawan\\n- **Threats**: Hunting, bycatch, seagrass habitat loss\\n- **Conservation**: Marine protected areas, community-based conservation\\n- **Fun fact**: \"Sea cow\", herbivorous marine mammal, related sa manatees!\\n\\n**Birds (Ibon):**\\n\\n**1. Philippine Cockatoo (Cacatua haematuropygia):**\\n- **Status**: Critically Endangered\\n- **Population**: Less than 1,000 individuals\\n- **Location**: Palawan, Tawi-Tawi\\n- **Threats**: Pet trade, habitat loss\\n- **Conservation**: Katala Foundation, community-based conservation\\n\\n**2. Visayan Warty Pig (Sus cebifrons):**\\n- **Status**: Critically Endangered\\n- **Location**: Panay, Negros\\n- **Population**: Less than 500\\n- **Threats**: Hunting, habitat loss\\n- **Fun fact**: May \"punk rock\" hairstyle during mating season!\\n\\n**3. Rufous Hornbill (Buceros hydrocorax):**\\n- **Status**: Vulnerable\\n- **Location**: Luzon, Mindanao\\n- **Threats**: Hunting, deforestation\\n- **Fun fact**: \"Kalaw\" - may loud call na naririnig ng 1 km away!\\n\\n**Reptiles at Amphibians:**\\n\\n**1. Philippine Crocodile (Crocodylus mindorensis):**\\n- **Status**: Critically Endangered\\n- **Population**: Less than 100 sa wild\\n- **Location**: Mindanao, Luzon\\n- **Threats**: Hunting, habitat destruction, fear\\n- **Conservation**: Mabuwaya Foundation, community education\\n- **Fun fact**: Endemic sa Pilipinas, mas maliit kaysa saltwater crocodile!\\n\\n**2. Panay Monitor Lizard (Varanus mabitang):**\\n- **Status**: Endangered\\n- **Location**: Panay Island lang\\n- **Threats**: Hunting, habitat loss\\n- **Fun fact**: Fruit-eating monitor lizard - rare sa mga bayawak!\\n\\n**Marine Species:**\\n\\n**1. Whale Shark (Butanding) (Rhincodon typus):**\\n- **Status**: Endangered\\n- **Location**: Donsol, Oslob, Tubbataha\\n- **Threats**: Bycatch, boat strikes, hunting (historically)\\n- **Conservation**: Ecotourism, protected areas\\n- **Fun fact**: Pinakamalaking isda sa mundo, pero kumakain lang ng plankton!\\n\\n**2. Hawksbill Sea Turtle (Pawikan) (Eretmochelys imbricata):**\\n- **Status**: Critically Endangered\\n- **Threats**: Poaching ng eggs at shells, bycatch, habitat loss\\n- **Conservation**: Protected nesting beaches, marine sanctuaries\\n\\n**3. Giant Clams (Tridacna spp.):**\\n- **Status**: Vulnerable to Endangered (depende sa species)\\n- **Threats**: Overharvesting, aquarium trade, habitat destruction\\n- **Conservation**: Marine protected areas, breeding programs\\n\\n**Plants:**\\n\\n**1. Jade Vine (Strongylodon macrobotrys):**\\n- **Status**: Endangered\\n- **Location**: Tropical forests\\n- **Threats**: Deforestation\\n- **Fun fact**: May unique turquoise-jade na kulay, isa sa pinaka-rare na bulaklak sa mundo!\\n\\n**2. Rafflesia (Rafflesia spp.):**\\n- **Status**: Endangered\\n- **Location**: Forest floors\\n- **Threats**: Habitat loss, over-collection\\n- **Fun fact**: Pinakamalaking bulaklak sa mundo, walang stems o leaves, parasitic!\\n\\n**Conservation Efforts sa Pilipinas:**\\n\\n**1. Protected Areas:**\\n- **National Integrated Protected Areas System (NIPAS)**: 240+ protected areas\\n- **Wildlife sanctuaries**: Safe havens para sa endangered species\\n- **Marine protected areas**: 1,600+ MPAs\\n\\n**2. Breeding Programs:**\\n- **Philippine Eagle Center**: Captive breeding at release\\n- **Tamaraw Conservation Program**: Breeding farm sa Mindoro\\n- **Crocodile Farming Institute**: Breeding at research\\n\\n**3. Laws at Policies:**\\n- **Wildlife Resources Conservation and Protection Act (RA 9147)**: Penalty para sa hunting at trade ng endangered species\\n- **National Caves and Cave Resources Management and Protection Act**: Protects bat habitats\\n- **Fisheries Code**: Protects marine species\\n\\n**4. Community-Based Conservation:**\\n- **Bantay Dagat**: Marine patrols\\n- **Bantay Gubat**: Forest patrols\\n- **Ecotourism**: Alternative livelihood, incentive para sa conservation\\n\\n**5. Research at Monitoring:**\\n- **Population surveys**: Track species numbers\\n- **Habitat assessment**: Evaluate ecosystem health\\n- **Genetic studies**: Understand diversity at connectivity\\n\\n**Paano Ka Makakatulong?**\\n\\n**1. Huwag Bumili ng Illegal Wildlife Products:**\\n- Avoid coral jewelry, turtle shells, animal skins\\n- Huwag bumili ng wild animals bilang pets\\n- Report illegal wildlife trade sa DENR\\n\\n**2. Support Conservation Organizations:**\\n- Donate sa Philippine Eagle Foundation, WWF Philippines, Haribon Foundation\\n- Volunteer sa conservation activities\\n- Adopt-an-animal programs\\n\\n**3. Practice Responsible Tourism:**\\n- Huwag hawakan o disturb ang wildlife\\n- Follow guidelines sa protected areas\\n- Support eco-friendly tour operators\\n- \"Leave no trace\" principles\\n\\n**4. Reduce Your Environmental Impact:**\\n- Bawasan ang plastic use (marine species protection)\\n- Mag-save ng kuryente (reduce climate change)\\n- Plant native trees (habitat restoration)\\n\\n**5. Spread Awareness:**\\n- Share knowledge about endangered species\\n- Educate others about conservation\\n- Use social media para sa advocacy\\n- Join school environmental clubs\\n\\n**Mga Tanong para Pagnilayan:**\\n\\n1. Bakit importante ang biodiversity? Ano ang mangyayari kung mawala ang isang species?\\n2. Alin sa mga endangered species ang pinaka-interesante sa iyo? Bakit?\\n3. Paano nakakatulong ang ecotourism sa conservation? May downsides ba ito?\\n\\n**Fun Facts:**\\n- Ang **Philippine Eagle** ay kailangan ng **7,000-13,000 hectares** ng forest para sa isang breeding pair - kaya ang habitat protection ay critical!\\n- Ang **Tamaraw** ay endemicsa Mindoro lang - wala sila sa ibang lugar sa mundo! Kung mawala sila sa Mindoro, extinct na sila forever!\\n- Ang **Philippine Tarsier** ay may eyes na **150x mas malaki** kaysa sa human eyes relative sa body size!\\n- Ang **Dugong** ay tinatawag na \"sea cow\" dahil kumakain sila ng seagrass - isang dugong kumakain ng **40 kg ng seagrass** araw-araw!\\n- Ang **Jade Vine** ay pollinated ng mga **bats** lang - kung mawala ang bats, mawawala din ang vine!\\n\\nAno ang pwede mong gawin para makatulong sa protection ng endangered species sa Pilipinas? May alam ka bang local species na nanganganib?"
